Loose rules ([@@@css]) keep source order and come before every atom, even
when the file writes an atom first.

  $ cat > a.ml <<EOT
  > [@@@css.atoms [("_a", ["._a{color:red}"], 0, 0, 1, [])]]
  > [@@@css ".global-one{color:blue}"]
  > EOT

  $ cat > b.ml <<EOT
  > [@@@css ".global-two{color:green}"]
  > EOT

  $ styled-ppx.generate a.ml b.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  .global-one{color:blue}
  .global-two{color:green}
  ._a{color:red}
